      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T08:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Connection is not \"tied\" to address, that\u0027s why we have connection handle as identifier. If multiple clients request connection using different RPAs, X, Y, Z, I wouldn\u0027t mind returning same handle with different addresses to each of them.\n\nOr you have to specify in callback what type of address will we return, but it can change, i.e. if you pair device on other transport.",
